# L §6.1 What same does: "a place two of them book (one place, or places stated same) takes it at the point of the
# last of them in the day's order (§5.14.2), since a decision's amount is known only at its point"; L §5.19, E §4.2:
# observations are booked in step 1, decisions at their point in step 3. sweep is a decision (it reads konto's running
# balance); the bank's row r1 is stated same as its March instance, so r1's ends wait for sweep's point: sweep reads
# konto before r1 (300.00 PLN), both give 300.00 PLN on 2026-03-31, and the movement is booked once there. By L §5.10's
# bal: konto 300.00 - 300.00 = 0.00 PLN, savings 0.00 + 300.00 = 300.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input bank: observed
input sweep_day: date

move sweep: transfers
  on sweep_day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount bal(konto)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  sweep_day = 2026-03-31 "plan"
  opening[konto] = 300.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[savings] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version stmt
  cite s
  known 2026-04-02
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-03-31, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to savings amount 300.00 PLN) "linia 1"
  same bank[r1] = sweep

ask k: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask sv: bal(savings, 2026-12-31)
=== expect
k: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
sv: 300.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-20
